    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVIIII. Gif hwa sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.2"/> deaðes scyldig ⁊ he cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.16"/> geierne, hæbbe his feorh ⁊ bete, swa him ryht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.17"/> wisige.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVIIII. Gif hwa sie deaþes scyldig ⁊ cirican geærne, habbe his feorh ⁊ bete, swa him ryht wisie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLIX. Gif hwa sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.1"/> deaðes scyldig ⁊ cirican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.10"/> geyrne, hæbbe his feorh ⁊ bete, swa him ryht wisie.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ciricsocnu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gyf hwá sy deaðes scyldig ⁊ he cyricean g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>yrne, hæbbe his feorh ⁊ béte, swa him riht wisie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis sit mortis reus et ad ecclesiam confugiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.12"/>, uitam habeat et emendet, sicut rectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.13"/> sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.14"/> consulet.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_5.lnote.oe.15"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="38" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ciricsocnum.] Gif hwa sie deaðes scyldig ⁊ he cirican geierne<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_5.attnote.fn.1"/>, hæbbe his feorh ⁊ bete, swa him ryht wisige.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="374" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XLVIIII} Gif swa he deaðes scyldig ⁊ he cirican geierne, hæbbe his feorh ⁊ bete, swa him ryht wisige.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand Todes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_5.lnote.de.1"/> schuldig ist und er eine Kirche erreicht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_5.lnote.de.2"/>, so behalte er sein Leben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_5.lnote.de.3"/> und büsse, wie ihm [das] die Rechtsordnung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_5.lnote.de.4"/> zuweist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone is liable to death and he reaches a church, let him keep his life and pay compensation as the law directs him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="39" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone is liable to the death penalty, and he flees to a church, his life shall be spared and he shall pay such compensation as he is directed [to pay] by legal decision.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="400" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone is liable to the death penalty and he reaches a church, he is to retain his life and to compensate as the law directs him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="375" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone has commited an offense for which he owes his life and he flees into a church, let him keep his life and make restitution according to how [judgment of] law directs him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="366"><label>earlier hinted at</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_1">Abt 1</ref> <quote>to establish the right of sanctuary (earlier hinted at in Æthelberht §6)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="375"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-13">Af El 13</ref> <quote>Compare MP §13 and Alfred §5.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="375"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5">Af 5</ref> <quote>Compare MP §13 and Alfred §5.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="236"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-13">Af El 13</ref> <quote>Compare Ine §5.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>revises (rights of the Church)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_2">Af 2–2.1</ref> <quote>sanctuary was given a time-limit; on the other, its range was extended ... (n. 79: Af 2 – 2:1, 5 – 5:4, 6 – 6:1; Ine 5 – 5:1, 6:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>revises (rights of the Church)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5">Af 5–5.4</ref> <quote>sanctuary was given a time-limit; on the other, its range was extended ... (n. 79: Af 2 – 2:1, 5 – 5:4, 6 – 6:1; Ine 5 – 5:1, 6:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="297"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_5">Af 5</ref> <quote>Cf. Ine §5.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><label>revises (rights of the Church)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_6">Af 6–6.1</ref> <quote>theft from a church was additionally penalized (n. 79: Af 2 – 2:1, 5 – 5:4, 6 – 6:1; Ine 5 – 5:1, 6:1)</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fug. <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fug. Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">aus Co Or; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">from Co Or; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">91</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-luerit <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-luerit Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor</hi> an <hi rend="italic">ein Buchst. ausradirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a letter erased before an</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vor</hi> e <hi rend="italic">ein Buchst. ausradirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a letter erased before e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyricean geyrne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyricean geyrne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">90</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">riht <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">riht Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Asyl 4. 6f. 13</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Asyl 4. 6f. 13</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘erreitet’ Bu; <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Af 5³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘reaches by riding’ Bu; <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Af 5³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Auch vor Verstümmelung ist er sicher, laut des folgenden <hi rend="italic">gebete.</hi> Im Agsä. Recht alternieren peinliche Strafe und Geldbusse; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 169. 186. Mit Unrecht meint er, königliche Begnadigung müsse erst noch hinzutreten</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">He is safe from mutilation too, according to the following <hi rend="italic">gebete.</hi> In A.-S. law corporal punishment and monetary compensation alternate; Schreuer <hi rend="italic">Verbrechenskonk.</hi> 169. 186. He is wrong in thinking that a royal pardon must also be added</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_5.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">69</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">bessere Übs.: ‘Gericht(surteil)’. Auch Karls d. Gr. <hi rend="italic">Capit. Sax.</hi> 2 (ed. Boretius 68) schützt zwar dem Asylerreicher <hi rend="italic">vitam et membra; emendet autem quantum fuerit iudicatum</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">better translation: ‘court (judgment)’. Charlemagne’s <hi rend="italic">Capit. Sax.</hi> 2 (ed. Boretius 68) likewise secures to the man who reaches sanctuary <hi rend="italic">vitam et membra; emendet autem quantum fuerit iudicatum</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_5.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">38</biblScope></bibl><label>geierne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">geærne</hi>. Bu.</seg></note>
      </div>
